% Bibliography conventions for this project:
% Keep exactly five fields, in this order: title, author, booktitle, year, url.
% Store the publication venue in booktitle, including for journal articles.
% Preserve the appropriate entry type and existing citation key; reuse keys.
% Use a conference's full name followed by its standard abbreviation:
%   International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)
%   International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)
%   Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)
%   Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)
%   Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)
%   AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)
%   Conference on Language Modeling (COLM)
% Use identical spelling and abbreviations for the same venue in every entry.
% Keep Findings and track distinctions; place track names before the abbreviation.
% Use full journal names, with standard abbreviations where applicable.
% For preprints, use exactly: arXiv preprint arXiv:2609.04565
% Replace the example identifier with the paper's actual arXiv identifier.
% Use a conference venue only when acceptance/publication has been verified.
% Use the cited version's year and prefer its official publication URL.
% Do not add journal, pages, volume, number, doi, publisher, or other fields.
% The local BST accepts booktitle for articles and sorts cited entries;
% entry position here does not determine the order in the printed References.
% Recency preferences (relative to the current calendar year and month):
% In principle, cite papers from the current year and the preceding two years
% (e.g., 2024--2026 when the current year is 2026).
% Prefer current-year papers to account for more than 50% of distinct cited papers.
% Aim for at least six distinct cited papers published or first released during
% the current calendar month or the previous calendar month, combined.
% These are rolling preferences, not fixed date cutoffs; verify publication or
% first-release dates rather than using access dates or later revision dates.
% Apply these preferences to papers actually cited in the manuscript, not all
% entries stored in this file; prioritize relevance and retain essential older work.

